{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786972779,"nonce":"RKOa5IemNkVTWjriAZ9X9YrTl18=","message":"Landed in `3fca990`.\n\n`--oto-wash` exists in the non-themed `:root` block of `tokens.css`, derived as `color-mix(in oklab, var(--oto-text) 6%, transparent)` so both palettes are correct from one declaration. `tokens.test.ts` and `contrast.test.ts` are both green and neither was taught about it — the placement is what keeps it out of their reach, exactly as the ticket predicted.\n\nFour more tints landed with it rather than one, and the extra ones are worth saying out loud:\n\n- `--oto-wash-heading` / `--oto-wash-heading-accent` at 12%, which the heading ticket needed.\n- `--oto-wash-rule` / `--oto-wash-rule-accent` at **48%**, which nothing predicted. It came out of looking at the rendered screen: the tapered underline sits *beside* text rather than behind it, so it owes contrast nothing, and at 12% a 4 px stroke is not a quiet brush — it is an invisible one whose surviving fraction reads as a `border-bottom`. §M.9 states the split as occupancy rather than taste.\n\nThe `@utility` is `oto-ink`. It carries the fill, the mask layers, `pointer-events: none`, `user-select: none` and the `forced-colors: active` guard in one place. `Ink.tsx` sits in front of it and carries the two things a stylesheet cannot: `aria-hidden`, and the `/motifs/` URL as a typed union so a misspelt motif is a compile error rather than a flat rectangle of wash. It also exports `clearColumn`, which is the carve-out geometry the other three tickets lean on.\n\n`web/public/motifs/` holds five assets and a README. Every one carries `preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"` and the README says why beside them. Nothing in `web/src` uses a hardcoded `rgba()` for decorative ink.\n\nTwo gates that were not asked for and are the reason to trust the rest: `ink.test.ts` recomputes every composite §M.9 publishes and fails in **both** directions — a ✅ that stops clearing its floor is an accessibility defect, and the ❌ row that justifies the whole carve-out design would become fiction-that-reads-as-evidence if it ever started passing. It also fails on a motif in the union with no asset behind it, on an asset missing `preserveAspectRatio`, and on a tint that drifts into a `[data-theme]` block.\n\nSPEC §M.9 and ADR 0035 record the rules, the placements refused, and the measured composites.","files":null}]}